  "sectionFacts": [
    "Three gabled bays of varying widths share a timber-framed building clad with vertical corrugated iron panels.",
    "The southeast face has a three-lobed original parapet and lettering. The separate Caroline Street corner awning wraps around its southwest end.",
    "Masonry and timber stumps hold the main floor approximately one metre above Landsborough Street. The two street entrances are on Caroline Street.",
    "The middle roof has two circular ridge vents. Timber doors and ventilating sashes sit under narrow rear awnings."
  ],
